class:: LatoocarfianSonify
summary:: Explicit Latoocarfian-map clock and level sonifier
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/LatoocarfianMap, Classes/HenonSonify

description::

Wrapping the trigonometric Latoocarfian map, this explicit sonifier evaluates the chaotic sine-based recurrence at the audio sample rate. The natural oscillation of the underlying equations behaves somewhat like chaotic, self-modulating FM synthesis when pushed into the audio domain. This provides an instantly usable, rich chaotic oscillator bursting with complex, shifting harmonics and inharmonic metallic overtones.

Uses link::Classes/LatoocarfianMap::'s documented recurrence, explicitly folding selected coordinates into iteration frequency and bipolar level. Frequency is bounded and at most one iteration occurs per sample.

Interpolation is hold, linear, or cubic Hermite. Unlike LatoocarfianMap, this class deliberately maps mathematical state into an audio signal.

subsection:: Visualizing the internal dynamics

See link::Classes/LatoocarfianMap:: for the recurrence's static portrait and exact-state live view. The sonifier does not expose its internal coordinates, so a separately clocked copy should not be presented as the orbit producing the sound.

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: minFreq
Mapped minimum iteration hertz.
argument:: maxFreq
Mapped maximum iteration hertz.
argument:: clockLo
Lower clock-coordinate folding bound.
argument:: clockHi
Upper clock-coordinate folding bound.
argument:: outputLo
Lower level-coordinate folding bound.
argument:: outputHi
Upper level-coordinate folding bound.
argument:: clockIndex
Init-rate clock coordinate: 0 x, 1 y.
argument:: outputIndex
Init-rate level coordinate: 0 x, 1 y.
argument:: interp
Init-rate 0 hold, 1 linear, 2 cubic Hermite.
argument:: a
y-equation sine coefficient.
argument:: b
x-equation sine coefficient.
argument:: c
x-equation second sine weight.
argument:: d
y-equation second sine weight.
argument:: x0
Initial x state.
argument:: y0
Initial y state.
argument:: reset
Restore map, phase, and interpolation state.
argument:: mul
Output multiplier.
argument:: add
Output offset.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ LatoocarfianSonify.ar * 0.08 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ LatoocarfianSonify.ar(40, 6000, interp: 1) * 0.08 }.play
)
::

code::
// Chaotic Trigonometric Bell
(
{
    var env, sig;
    // Interlocking sines fold into complex inharmonic overtones
    env = EnvGen.kr(Env.perc(0.01, 1.0), doneAction: 2);
    sig = LatoocarfianSonify.ar(300 * env + 100);
    Pan2.ar(LeakDC.ar(sig) * env * 0.2)
}.play;
)
::
